<div class="page-heading">
  <div>
    <h1>ERP connections</h1>
    <p>Five modules use one database: mindafresh_db.</p>
  </div>
</div>
<section class="panel">
  <div class="panel-heading">
    <h2>PeoplePay · HR <span class="badge">Owner</span></h2>
    <span class="muted">Port 3004</span>
  </div>
  <p class="panel-copy">
    Writes departments, employees, users, leave_requests, payroll_runs and
    payroll_items. All modules refer to the same employees.id.
  </p>
</section>
<section class="panel">
  <div class="panel-heading">
    <h2>Attendance <span class="badge green">Read only</span></h2>
    <span class="muted">Port 3003</span>
  </div>
  <p class="panel-copy">
    PeoplePay reads attendance_logs and holidays to compute payroll. The
    Attendance module owns timekeeping and corrections.
  </p>
</section>
<section class="panel">
  <div class="panel-heading">
    <h2>Accounting & Finance <span class="badge green">Read only</span></h2>
    <span class="muted">Port 3005</span>
  </div>
  <p class="panel-copy">
    Accounting reads approved payroll, posts journal_entries and writes
    salary_releases. PeoplePay shows posted and paid status from those records.
  </p>
</section>
<section class="panel">
  <div class="panel-heading">
    <h2>Point of Sale and Online Shop</h2>
    <span class="muted">Ports 3002 and 3001</span>
  </div>
  <p class="panel-copy">
    Staff use the shared users and employees tables through authService. Shop
    customer accounts remain separate. No employee data is copied between
    modules.
  </p>
</section>
<div class="note">
  These are database integration contracts, not a live health check of the other
  module servers.
</div>
